; ear-tongue-ring.fk — the tongue lane's bell, rung from outside the lane.
;
; A fork costs what the forking process has TOUCHED, not what it has mapped: ten host-exec calls
; measured 3.4 ms each before the weights were opened, 3.6 ms after `dm-open` mapped them, and
; 100 ms each after eight decode steps had walked the whole 1.3 GB blob — the page tables the
; decode made resident are copied on every fork. The lane used to ring its own bell by forking a
; shell per frame, so every frame cost 100 ms where the four decode steps behind it cost 60.
;
; So the ringing lives here, in a process that has never touched a weight. It watches the spool's
; size and writes the bell natively — `sbt-ring`, one byte, no shell. Blocking on a reader is
; RIGHT for this process: it exists only to ring, and while it waits the spool keeps growing, so
; the reader that finally arrives is woken once for everything that landed. The lane stands this
; cell at open, before its first step, when a fork is still cheap.
;
; stdin line 1: run seconds (blank -> 86400). The lane wraps it in tools/ftimeout, so a bell that
; never finds a reader ends with the lane rather than outliving it. Preflight must not run it: with
; no stdin it stands for a day, and its whole body is the standing.
; preflight-exec: forbidden
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/spool-bell-transport.fk form/form-stdlib/line-grammar.fk
(do
    (defn tr-spool () ".hearth/ear.spool")
    (defn tr-bell () ".hearth/ear.spool.bell")
    ; the spool's size is the whole signal: grown means frames landed
    (defn tr-size () (do (let n (file_size (tr-spool))) (if (lt n 0) 0 n)))
    (defn tr-go (mark deadline)
        (if (gt (now_unix_ms) deadline) 0
            (do (let sz (tr-size))
                (if (gt sz mark)
                    (do (sbt-ring (tr-bell)) (tr-go sz deadline))
                    (do (host_sleep_ms 15) (tr-go mark deadline))))))
    (let secs (do (let l (read_line)) (if (nothing? l) 86400 (do (let t (trim l)) (if (eq (str_len t) 0) 86400 (str_to_int t))))))
    (print_str (str_concat "tongue bell standing for " (str_concat (int_to_str secs) " s")))
    (tr-go (tr-size) (add (now_unix_ms) (mul 1000 secs)))
    1)
